WEBVTT

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.620
Kazuma!

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:17.370
Grandpa?

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:21.720
Grandpa!

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:31.480
Grandpa!

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.670
Huh? Isn’t this Kazuma?

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:36.110
Kazuma is on television!

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:38.690
Kazuma has...

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:42.770
My Kazuma has returned...

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:44.070
It’s the television. Television.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:47.900
Kazuma!

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:52.320
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.200
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.500
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.860
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:05.130
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:08.810
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:22.430
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:26.020
Yakitate!! Japan
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:27.350
Yakitate!! Japan

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:33.990
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:41.870
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:49.580
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:57.050
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:06.430
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:15.190
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:19.450
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.450
is the light of only you.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:26.190
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:31.040
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:38.720
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:42.560
Kawachi Kai!!

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.370
The Solar Gauntlet!

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:48.400
But why were you on television?

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:50.490
There was a bit of this and that and such...

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:53.160
And we got onto a program that
was to air about two weeks ago.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:56.150
Huh? You’ve become quite the
famous one, too, haven’t you?

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:58.500
I’m happy...

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:01.130
But aside from that, is Grandpa okay?

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:01.670
Kazuma...

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:02.730
Huh?
Kazuma...

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:03.800
Kazuma.

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:07.420
He’s twitchy and jerky, so it seems
that he’s slowly coming back...

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:10.090
I think we’ve leapt this hurdle
for now. It’s all right.

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:11.120
That’s a relief.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.010
Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:13.890
Later, then...

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:18.430
How old is your grandpa, Kazuma?

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:21.630
He’s eighty-nine...
Next year he’ll be exactly ninety.

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:26.350
Then, he’s ten years younger than my grandfather.

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:28.370
Our victory!

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:30.030
Of what, I wonder?

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:33.850
That very grandfather has sent over

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:36.560
this for the recent employees.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:37.860
Oh! The red papers!

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:39.860
It’s already that time?

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:41.580
What’s that?

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:45.570
It’s the draft notice for all of Pantasia’s newcomers.

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:47.420
For the newcomers?

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:48.120
Yeah.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.380
For the Pantasia group...

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:55.010
It’s a challenge that brings together the new-
comers from all 128 stores around the country.

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:59.570
The objective is to battle it out seriously, and to
measure how your skills compare to each other.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:05.410
By the way, I was the winner eleven years ago!

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:07.050
But you were forced out of the capital.

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:14.070
Tsukino, I believe that eight years ago, you
were among the best three, weren’t you?

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:14.810
Yes.

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:18.370
It was really amazing to see someone still carrying her school backpack

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:20.040
on the winner’s podium.

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:22.920
You all are amazing, aren’t you?

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:24.160
By the way...

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.170
I caught a bit of rudeness that needs to be put down!

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:30.010
The two of you really are amazing, aren’t you?

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:33.160
All right, so I flunked the preliminaries.

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:36.170
For the newcomers, huh?

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:37.810
By the way...

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:41.140
Do you gain any privileges if you win?

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:43.690
The winner gets an award
of one million yen.

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:46.810
You also get a sabbatical in France.

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:50.680
In addition, you get the special treatment
of possible placement at the main store.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:52.520
Is that true?

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:55.950
All right then!

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:58.700
I’m going to win.

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:00.790
And you’ll be... number two.

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:02.120
Good luck!

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:03.960
Okay! I’m number two!

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:05.420
Number two?

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:07.910
This may be like throwing cold
water over your plans, but...

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:11.910
If appears that, compared to previous years,
we have a lot more newcomers this year.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:15.500
The total number of newcomers from all 128 stores is...

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:17.800
an incredible 512!

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:20.310
It’s about three times the number we usually have.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:23.810
Since the group as a whole is promising,

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:26.400
they must have drastically reduced the numbers.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.760
But for the two of you, this is
quite unfortunate, isn’t it?

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:32.970
Frankly, you probably won’t make
it through the preliminaries.

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:35.580
512!

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:39.240
Is that a large number?

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:42.020
Didn’t he just say that it’s three
times the usual number?

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:45.740
Then, it’ll be all right if we work three
times harder than normal, right?

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:49.240
Man... when it comes to his optimism...

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:52.240
He doesn’t seem to feel
any pressure at all...

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:55.840
So, what do we have to do for the preliminaries?

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:57.720
It’s different each year.

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:00.750
So, let’s see here...
This year’s theme is...

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:04.180
Din... din...

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:08.770
It’s dinner bread! Bread! Bread!

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:12.270
What? What’s with the
exaggerated reaction?

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:14.440
It’s just dinner bread, isn’t it?

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:15.950
“Within the regular conditions of a room:”

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:19.910
“Room temperature of 23 degrees,
and humidity of 55%...”

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:22.280
“make a bread that will not grow mold for three weeks!”

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:24.040
“You get one week for the test.”

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:27.040
“And it goes without saying that you cannot
use artificial ingredients like preservatives!”

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:30.080
This is what’s written.
Can you call this “mere dinner bread?”

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:33.590
Mere dinner bread...

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:35.790
Long lasting dinner bread, is it?

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:40.930
Mold exists naturally all across the
Earth, in all kinds of places.

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:43.850
A temperature above 20°C is sufficient
to allow it to germinate.

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:48.130
Not only food, but glass and metal could
be used as a source of nutrients, as well.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:51.810
If we were to put it into the fridge, that’s one thing...

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:56.430
Can you really make a bread that’d remain good
for three weeks under normal room conditions?

00:06:56.870 --> 00:07:00.460
And asking us not to use
preservatives is crazy!

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:03.020
You can definitely call it
a crazy theme.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:03.650
But...

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:08.460
Poor students living on their own, or manga artists...

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:10.780
There are plenty of customers in the world who’d eat

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:13.000
2-3 weeks leftover bread
without a second thought.

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:15.130
Amongst the molds that grow on bread,

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:15.290
there are also those that can release
deadly poisons, called mucotoxins.

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:18.130
Mucotoxins

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:21.210
And these toxins are not nullified upon heating!

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:21.220
Mucotoxins
And these toxins are not nullified upon heating!

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:23.500
Being unaware of such things,
Mucotoxins

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:26.400
people think it’s all right to just take off the mold...

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:31.050
And end up eating it...

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:34.010
That’s why...

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:39.520
We have to work hard to make a bread that’s
just little more delicious, and a little more safe.

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:42.780
Well, I see what the reasoning behind the theme is,

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:46.160
but the question’s whether or not you
can really make such a bread.

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:47.270
Right, Azuma?

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:50.290
Yeah, you can...

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:52.530
It’s <i>Japan</i> #32.

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:55.120
What’s with that outfit?

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:56.210
I’m going to get it.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:00.790
I’m going to search for
<i>Japan</i> #32’s ingredients.

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:03.000
I’ll get Kawachi’s share, as well...

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.720
Hey!

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:07.760
Wait up, will you, Azuma?

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:10.760
It’s still working hours for the store...

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:13.510
That idiot...
Where does he plan to go?

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:16.140
Azuma seems to have thought of something, hasn’t he?

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.890
That seems to be so, but...

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:21.430
It probably isn’t anything that could be of any use...

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:23.640
Oh, you don’t think so?

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:29.280
But, I’m all excited that he might
do something wonderful again.

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:31.780
I know!

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:33.570
I know!

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:36.540
He’ll do something amazing again.

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:41.130
And he probably plans to share that with me, as well...

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:46.540
With that, the two of us may even
be able to pass the preliminaries.

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:50.050
However, I want to be able to win with my own abilities.

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:53.630
And I want to be chosen to go
to the main store for my skill.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:57.260
I don’t want to go through something like
that time with the croissants again.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:00.600
For that, I have to be able to win against Azuma.

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:05.480
But... what can I do?

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:07.190
I don’t know.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:11.190
I neither have an idea to surpass him,

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:12.860
nor Solar Hands.

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:15.860
Kawachi-san...

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:21.250
We have a customer who’s troubled...

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:23.500
because she can’t get through.

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:26.000
I’ll come later...

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:30.880
There, there...

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:38.970
Do you want Solar Hands?

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:41.390
I know a way...

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:45.190
of attaining Solar Hands...

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:49.030
Wha...? What?

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:01.030
Don’t mess with me!

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:03.620
Solar Hands are a hereditary trait.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:06.580
There’s no way to get them, aside from being reborn.

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:10.250
Then... wouldn’t it be best to be reborn?

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.670
As Kawachi Kai.

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:15.230
Note: “Kai” means “to alter” or “to reform.”

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:17.440
Me? Kai?!
Note: “Kai” means “to alter” or “to reform.”

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:18.140
Note: “Kai” means “to alter” or “to reform.”

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:26.080
If the Solar Hands were to become mine...

00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:29.210
If I could really get them...

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:31.230
I might...

00:10:32.370 --> 00:10:34.730
I might be able to fight it out with him...

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:43.450
Hmm... it seems you have decided to believe in it...

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:45.890
In what I told you...

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:52.230
It’s for real, isn’t it?

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:54.060
Yeah...

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:54.940
Somewhat...

00:10:55.430 --> 00:10:58.920
However... please, do not run off
in the middle at all.

00:10:59.480 --> 00:11:03.240
If so, Solar Hands will not come to you.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:06.930
Asuzakawa Sports Club

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:08.930
What?

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:14.290
What in the world is this?

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:16.440
If you go to a pool, you swim.

00:11:16.830 --> 00:11:21.330
From today onward, please swim about 10km
twice a day, in the morning and at night.

00:11:21.330 --> 00:11:22.460
Don’t mess with me.

00:11:22.460 --> 00:11:24.750
I want Solar Hands!

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:27.260
I don’t want a swimming medal.

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:29.550
I’m not telling you to improve your swimming.

00:11:29.550 --> 00:11:30.460
But, then...

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:33.920
You talk too much.

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:37.810
Hey!

00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:39.530
What’s with pushing me–

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:43.950
What’s with this float?

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:46.530
The float is sinking me...

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:48.190
It’s heavy.

00:11:48.190 --> 00:11:50.320
And I can’t use my legs at all either.

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:53.320
That may look like a float, but...

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:57.250
It’s designed to get heavier as it absorbs more moisture.

00:11:58.910 --> 00:12:00.580
Do you know about koshikeihou?

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:02.960
In the age of civil war,

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:07.550
they were soldiers who would swim while
wearing heavy armor and holding a spear.

00:12:08.590 --> 00:12:10.420
If you want Solar Hands,

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:14.690
then we must have you strengthen up enough
to be able to swim with the fake float.

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:20.810
I don’t know about civil war soldiers
needing to be strong or anything...

00:12:20.810 --> 00:12:22.520
I’m a baker.

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:24.270
I’m drowning!

00:12:24.270 --> 00:12:27.890
In order not to sink, you have no choice but to keep swimming, right?

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:30.030
Hang in there.

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:31.400
Oh, that’s right.

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:34.870
A scary SV person will be keeping watch over you, so...

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:37.400
There’s no giving up until you’ve done the 10km.

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:39.400
Well...

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:43.900
I think he’d probably save you if you looked
like you were really going to die.

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:45.420
Later!

00:12:50.760 --> 00:12:52.550
What are you doing?

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:52.950
What a horrible pose!

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:54.840
Horrible
pose
What a horrible pose!

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:57.050
I get it! It’s okay if I swim, right?
pose
Horrible

00:12:59.060 --> 00:13:01.050
What’s doing something like this going to get me?

00:13:01.850 --> 00:13:04.300
That woman! I’m going to get her.

00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:10.770
Manager, you were here as well,
were you?

00:13:10.770 --> 00:13:13.650
That was pretty nice of you, wasn’t it?

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:15.310
Well, that’s to be expected.

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:17.370
Why do you say that?

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:20.370
The branch to which the champion belongs will get...

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:22.280
one million yen in reward money.

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:24.820
You were also aiming for that money, weren’t you?

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:29.090
Well, since the budget does not
allocate much to our store,

00:13:29.090 --> 00:13:32.170
if one million was to come our way, then...
in addition to the latest style ovens,

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:34.830
we could remodel the entire store!

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:36.970
That... and this... and that...

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:39.260
If, for some reason, Azuma-san were to lose,

00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:42.060
we’d have to get Kawachi-san to do it in his place...

00:13:42.060 --> 00:13:43.840
And in order to do that...

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:46.090
How can you make me say
things like this?

00:13:46.900 --> 00:13:49.200
I won’t say that I don’t want the money.

00:13:50.610 --> 00:13:55.080
But having Kawachi-san help us out isn’t
something I thought of yesterday, or today.

00:13:55.700 --> 00:13:58.070
On the last day of the employment
exam for the main store...

00:13:58.070 --> 00:14:01.360
I’m a country boy, too...

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:05.360
I want to believe in the tears
I saw that day.

00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:14.100
No more...

00:14:16.930 --> 00:14:18.940
I guess it’s impossible.

00:14:19.430 --> 00:14:21.350
In the end... someone like me...

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:24.400
Are you going to give up, Kyousuke?

00:14:26.020 --> 00:14:27.320
This voice...

00:14:37.490 --> 00:14:38.900
Listen here, Kyousuke.

00:14:39.280 --> 00:14:42.650
Your father is going to get hired into
the Pantasia store for sure this time.

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:44.910
And the main store, at that!

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:46.460
I think it’ll be impossible again, though.

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:47.650
That’s right.

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:49.920
Don’t always be seeking unattainable dreams.

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:51.340
Look at reality.

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:52.660
Stop talking nonsense.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:55.370
The new item this time
is really amazing!

00:14:56.010 --> 00:14:59.350
The people of Pantasia group are
also going to be surprised!

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:03.760
Amongst the many young and talented examinees,

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:07.180
that middle-aged man would continue
trying for his dreams again and again,

00:15:07.180 --> 00:15:08.690
and he’d stand and face it...

00:15:10.940 --> 00:15:12.900
Sorry, Kyousuke.

00:15:12.900 --> 00:15:13.980
But you know what?

00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:17.280
Next year, however, I really will become
an employee of the Pantasia main store.

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:18.990
I’ll be able to make life easy for us all.

00:15:18.990 --> 00:15:20.440
It’s all right.

00:15:21.030 --> 00:15:24.330
If doesn’t matter whether or not you
become an employee of Pantasia...

00:15:24.330 --> 00:15:25.650
Don’t talk stupid.

00:15:26.370 --> 00:15:27.620
Listen up, Kyousuke.

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:29.120
You can’t ever give up.

00:15:29.120 --> 00:15:31.710
Even if you mess up and are always in muddy waters...

00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:33.660
If you don’t give up till the
very end, then...

00:15:34.840 --> 00:15:37.660
Someday, you’ll reach the end,
and be able to smile.

00:15:40.590 --> 00:15:41.670
Father.

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:43.220
Okay?

00:15:43.220 --> 00:15:45.060
You can’t ever give up.

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:47.140
Don’t ever forget this.

00:15:47.140 --> 00:15:48.570
Do you understand?

00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:53.060
He failed, and then failed again.

00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:55.860
But, my old man never gave up.

00:15:55.860 --> 00:15:57.830
And then, one day...

00:15:59.070 --> 00:16:00.770
The flames of his passion...

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:07.870
changed shape, and attacked our family.

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:10.000
Father!

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:13.210
Father is still inside.

00:16:13.210 --> 00:16:14.660
It’s dangerous, so stand back.

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:18.140
No!!!

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:24.390
The cause of the fire was the old oven’s air
chamber that he’d bought at his own expense.

00:16:24.390 --> 00:16:26.440
And the old man was inside when...

00:16:28.180 --> 00:16:31.180
The hard work that the old man put in every
day, like an idiot, into the dead of the night..

00:16:31.180 --> 00:16:35.320
That old man’s effort was all in vain
because of a stupid accident.

00:16:36.270 --> 00:16:40.030
After that, our family went to our mother’s home to live.

00:16:42.950 --> 00:16:45.440
Give up being a baker.
I will not forgive it.

00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:49.750
But I have to do something about
our dead father’s final regret.

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:51.830
He wasn’t much of a father, but...

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:54.030
I loved him!

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:56.780
So, I’m going to carry out his will.

00:16:58.210 --> 00:17:00.210
I’m going to become a baker.

00:17:00.210 --> 00:17:03.290
The best baker of Pantasia’s main store.

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:05.340
And then, I’ll save money and

00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:08.470
bring you, Kyouei, and Hiromi the share of happiness that Dad would have brought you.

00:17:08.470 --> 00:17:09.770
For sure!

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:14.220
I acted all cool, said a lot, and studied desperately.

00:17:14.770 --> 00:17:17.720
And what I gained was only knowledge.

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:20.720
Kawachi-san said this, as well.

00:17:21.150 --> 00:17:25.810
Maybe, in the end, I am my dumb father’s son after all, and don’t have any talent.

00:17:26.490 --> 00:17:28.950
I did a bad thing to Azuma, as well.

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:30.940
But I...

00:17:31.450 --> 00:17:34.250
wanted to win, to the point of death.

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:38.300
For my family’s sake, for my sake,
and for my father’s sake.

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:45.330
During that exam, what Kawachi-san
did was definitely wrong.

00:17:46.090 --> 00:17:49.010
If he had no feelings of remorse,

00:17:49.010 --> 00:17:52.020
and tried to get employed at the main store, then...

00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:55.840
I would have worked towards making
sure that he didn’t get employed.

00:17:56.440 --> 00:17:59.430
But he withdrew on his own.

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:03.890
He suppressed his passion and tenacity
towards working at the main store.

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:06.640
He gave in to the pangs of his conscience.

00:18:07.030 --> 00:18:10.780
And that time, I decided within my
heart that I would invite him

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:12.320
to the Tokyo southern branch.

00:18:13.450 --> 00:18:15.250
It’s because I decided that, if his passion towards

00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:17.880
getting into the main store were to
be guided in the right direction,

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:20.720
he’d become a great baker.

00:18:23.310 --> 00:18:24.830
This is another chance for him.

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:29.810
I’m beginning to space out.

00:18:30.350 --> 00:18:33.020
If I were to close my eyes like this...

00:18:33.020 --> 00:18:34.610
it would surely be easier...

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:37.760
Kyousuke.

00:18:38.370 --> 00:18:39.470
Kyousuke.

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:42.990
You can’t give up.

00:18:44.860 --> 00:18:46.220
Old man.

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:48.490
That’s right.

00:18:48.490 --> 00:18:50.190
I can’t give up.

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:55.170
My arms and my legs still...

00:18:56.710 --> 00:18:58.950
can move, somehow.

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:05.450
I have to keep going until the end.

00:19:07.420 --> 00:19:10.960
Wait, won’t you... Azuma!

00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:23.230
If Kawachi-san were to apply to the main
store once again based on his skill,

00:19:23.230 --> 00:19:25.310
I would happily cooperate with him.

00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:28.310
I understand what you’re thinking, Tsukino.

00:19:28.780 --> 00:19:33.810
However, to create the solar hands...
is not an easy thing.

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:37.040
If you were to increase the muscle
mass all over the body,

00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:40.330
then it would increase your basic metabolism,
as well as your body temperature.

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:42.460
You would have warm hands,

00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:46.840
produced due to the insulation of the armor that your muscles provide.

00:19:46.840 --> 00:19:50.760
The blood coming from the heart would
reach your extremities without cooling.

00:19:50.760 --> 00:19:53.390
If you do that, then, while you still wouldn’t
have Kazuma’s natural Solar Hands...

00:19:53.390 --> 00:19:56.610
you’d have warm hands produced due to the insulation of your muscles.

00:19:57.060 --> 00:20:00.010
You would have a Solar Gauntlet, so to speak.

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:01.590
Solar
Gauntlet
You would have a Solar Gauntlet, so to speak.

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:04.520
Well, that’s the theory of it, but...

00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:08.310
No regular workout could create that
much muscle in a short time.

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:13.770
Mokoyama and I both worked hard to get if, but...

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:16.980
We had the time for it.

00:20:17.450 --> 00:20:21.210
Whether or not a sudden surge of exercise
will be able to pull that off...

00:20:21.210 --> 00:20:25.340
depends on whether that passion and tenacity of
his is something that you can truly depend on.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:28.510
10km...

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:33.180
If I am to continue this, I’m going to die.

00:20:33.180 --> 00:20:34.170
That woman.

00:20:34.930 --> 00:20:36.170
Does she plan on killing me?

00:20:37.100 --> 00:20:38.430
No, but...

00:20:38.430 --> 00:20:42.730
My being able to stay in the Southern
branch is all thanks to Tsukino.

00:20:42.730 --> 00:20:45.680
I don’t think she’d be making me do this as a joke.

00:20:46.110 --> 00:20:48.190
I’m sure... I’m sure that it’s there.

00:20:48.190 --> 00:20:51.360
The signpost towards Solar Hands...

00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:53.940
hidden somewhere in this swimming exercise.

00:20:54.370 --> 00:20:55.650
Definitely.

00:20:56.490 --> 00:20:59.080
Wait up, everyone. Old man.

00:20:59.080 --> 00:21:01.450
Kawachi Kyousuke’s going to get stronger.

00:21:02.500 --> 00:21:04.660
As Kawachi Kai.

00:21:05.150 --> 00:21:06.910
Hey... wait a minute.

00:21:07.460 --> 00:21:13.410
Isn’t there some better name than that?

00:21:15.300 --> 00:21:16.350
There isn’t, is there?

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:18.350
Yeah, there isn’t.

00:21:18.350 --> 00:21:22.920
I have no doubts about Kawachi-san’s passion.

00:21:25.520 --> 00:21:29.430
For the one month before the competition,
I’m going to take care of Kawachi-san.

00:21:30.530 --> 00:21:34.430
In order to maximize his muscle development
by monitoring his food intake...

00:21:34.950 --> 00:21:37.660
With this, Azuma can’t let his
guard down either, can he?

00:21:38.450 --> 00:21:40.380
I’m sure Azuma-san will be all right.

00:21:40.870 --> 00:21:44.280
Moreover, I’m looking forward
to <i>Japan</i> #32.

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:50.010
I’m looking forward to that, too.

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:01.790
Hey, you. Stop.

00:22:02.850 --> 00:22:03.800
What is it?

00:22:04.640 --> 00:22:06.460
You’re underage, aren’t you?

00:22:06.460 --> 00:22:09.820
It’s past two in the morning.
Get back home quickly.

00:22:09.820 --> 00:22:12.230
No way. I’ve got somewhere to go.

00:22:12.230 --> 00:22:13.190
Somewhere to go?

00:22:13.190 --> 00:22:14.720
To Izu!

00:22:15.400 --> 00:22:19.030
What do you mean Izu?
This is Yokohama.

00:22:19.030 --> 00:22:22.160
There are no trains or anything running at this time.

00:22:22.160 --> 00:22:24.230
Hey, wait up.

00:22:25.540 --> 00:22:28.320
Mr. Policeman, is Izu this way?

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:34.620
Mr. Policeman, are you okay?
Hang in there!

00:22:39.370 --> 00:22:47.510
If I think of you, and even utter the clichéd phrase “I love you,”

00:22:48.080 --> 00:22:56.520
it makes such a nice sound, and you continue talking.

00:23:00.090 --> 00:23:07.530
The hopeless tears your bold self sometimes shows me form flag of truce.

00:23:08.830 --> 00:23:12.710
If nothing is said, then all the more,

00:23:12.900 --> 00:23:18.840
I just can’t look away. Things like sadness and pain...

00:23:18.840 --> 00:23:21.410
Well, that happens a lot in life, after all.

00:23:21.640 --> 00:23:25.550
When you casually say, “Do your best,” it gives me strength.

00:23:25.980 --> 00:23:30.320
Whenever your small back trembles, I will embrace you right away.

00:23:31.350 --> 00:23:34.160
Even if the scenery outside my window changes...

00:23:34.660 --> 00:23:38.860
Stay with me as you are, bad sleeping habits and all.

00:23:39.490 --> 00:23:44.030
If you sulk, and utter

00:23:44.300 --> 00:23:52.840
Even the clichéd “I hate you,” it comes across as the opposite.

00:23:53.240 --> 00:24:02.200
I will love you, no matter what. It’s just another Sunday to me.

00:24:06.380 --> 00:24:08.550
This isn’t good.
I’m all beat up.

00:24:08.550 --> 00:24:11.130
Will I really be able to make a bread that

00:24:11.130 --> 00:24:13.600
doesn’t grow mold by having Solar Gauntlets?

00:24:13.600 --> 00:24:15.850
Don’t be so irresolute!

00:24:15.850 --> 00:24:17.430
Next episode, Yakitate!! Japan.

00:24:17.430 --> 00:24:19.520
I won’t lose!!
I challenge you with my Osaka bread!

00:24:19.520 --> 00:24:20.850
Be sure to see it!

00:24:21.230 --> 00:24:23.600
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.600 --> 00:24:26.320
Amongst the molds, while we
have ones that make toxins,

00:24:26.320 --> 00:24:28.030
are ones that are not all bad!

00:24:28.030 --> 00:24:32.620
There are varieties that help in making
Japanese rice wine, miso, and cheese!
Note: Miso is a soy bean paste.

00:24:32.950 --> 00:24:34.040
Yeah, yeah!
